vist</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Grape</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Vocational rehabilitation of the socially disadvantaged long-term sick: inter-organizational co-operation between welfare state agencies</article-title><source>Scandinavian Journal of Public Health</source><year>1999</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10847664</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="r28"><label>28</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>&#x000d8;vretveit</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality in health promotion</article-title><source>Health Promotion International</source><year>1996</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>62</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="r29"><label>29</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quinn</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Intelligent enterprise: a knowledge and service based paradigm for industry</source><year>1992</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Free Press</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="r30"><label>30</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glendinning</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Breaking down barriers: integrating health and care services for older people in England</article-title><source>Health Policy</source><year>2003</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12849913</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="r31"><label>31</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><sour